src/device/common.h: guard the colltrace hw-id read on the gfx11/gfx12 families

Upstream skips the "s_getreg_b32 %0, hwreg(HW_REG_HW_ID)" read for
__gfx1100__/__gfx1101__/__gfx1102__/__gfx1200__/__gfx1201__ only. clang defines
__gfx11_generic__ and the family macro __GFX11__ for --offload-arch=gfx11-generic
(never __gfx1100__), so building for the generic targets still emits the asm and
lld fails the offload link of librccl.so with

    lld: error: ld-temp.o <inline asm>:1:25: invalid hardware register: not supported on this GPU

because HW_REG_HW_ID exists only through gfx9 (gfx10 aliases it to HW_REG_HW_ID1).
Guard on the family macros instead, which also covers gfx1103, gfx1150-1154 and
gfx1250 that the named-chip list misses. The traced data_0 field stays unset, as
it already does upstream for gfx1100 and gfx1200.

---
 src/device/common.h | 1 + 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/device/common.h b/src/device/common.h
index ada2eba..4425cbf 100644
--- a/src/device/common.h
+++ b/src/device/common.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
   { __atomic_store_n((DST), (SRC), __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST); }
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__gfx1100__) || defined(__gfx1101__) || defined(__gfx1102__) || defined(__gfx1200__) || defined(__gfx1201__)
+#if defined(__GFX11__) || defined(__GFX12__)
 #define __trace_hwreg()
 #else
 #define __trace_hwreg() \
